"use strict";(self.webpackChunktranzila_payment_for_woocommerce_pos_doc=self.webpackChunktranzila_payment_for_woocommerce_pos_doc||[]).push([[527],{3361(e,t,o){o.r(t),o.d(t,{_pageData:()=>a,default:()=>r});var n=o(641);const a=JSON.parse('{"path":"/tranzila-payment/installation.html","title":"Installation Guide","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"tranzila-payment/installation.md"}'),i={name:"installation.md"},r=(0,o(6262).A)(i,[["render",function(e,t,o,a,i,r){return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="installation-guide" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#installation-guide"><span>Installation Guide</span></a></h1><p>Setting up the <strong>Tranzila Payment for WooCommerce POS</strong> addon requires installing and activating the extension on your WordPress instance alongside the WooCommerce POS core plugin.</p><hr><h2 id="_1-system-requirements" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-system-requirements"><span>1. System Requirements</span></a></h2><p>Before installation, ensure your environment meets the following conditions:</p><ul><li><strong>WordPress:</strong> Version 5.0 or higher.</li><li><strong>WooCommerce:</strong> Version 5.0 or higher.</li><li><strong>POS for WooCommerce (Webkul):</strong> Active, licensed, and configured. <a href="https://wpdoc.webkul.com/pos-for-woocommerce/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Documentation &amp; Info</a>.</li><li><strong>PHP:</strong> Version 7.4 or higher.</li><li><strong>Tranzila Account:</strong> An active merchant terminal account with access to API endpoints.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="_2-installing-the-wordpress-plugin" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-installing-the-wordpress-plugin"><span>2. Installing the WordPress Plugin</span></a></h2><h3 id="method-1-wordpress-admin-dashboard-recommended" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#method-1-wordpress-admin-dashboard-recommended"><span>Method 1: WordPress Admin Dashboard (Recommended)</span></a></h3><p><strong>Step 1: Access Plugin Installation</strong></p><ol><li>Log in to your WordPress Admin Panel.</li><li>Navigate to: <strong>Plugins → Add New</strong>.</li><li>Click the <strong>Upload Plugin</strong> button at the top of the page.</li></ol><p><img src="/tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos/images/tranzila-payment/installation-add-new.webp" alt="Access Plugin Upload"></p><p><strong>Step 2: Upload the Plugin</strong></p><ol><li>Click the <strong>Choose File</strong> button.</li><li>Select the downloaded plugin ZIP file (e.g., <code>tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos.zip</code>).</li><li>Click <strong>Install Now</strong>.</li></ol><p><img src="/tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos/images/tranzila-payment/installation-upload-plugin.webp" alt="Upload Plugin Archive"></p><p><strong>Step 3: Activate the Plugin</strong></p><ol><li>After successful installation, click <strong>Activate Plugin</strong>.</li><li>Wait for the activation confirmation message to display in your WordPress plugin dashboard.</li></ol><p><img src="/tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos/images/tranzila-payment/installation-activate-plugin.webp" alt="Activate Plugin"></p><hr><h3 id="method-2-ftp-installation-alternative" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#method-2-ftp-installation-alternative"><span>Method 2: FTP Installation (Alternative)</span></a></h3><p><strong>Step 1: Prepare Files</strong></p><ol><li>Unzip the downloaded plugin package.</li><li>Extract the <code>tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos</code> folder.</li></ol><p><strong>Step 2: Upload via FTP</strong></p><ol><li>Connect to your server via FTP/SFTP client.</li><li>Navigate to the WordPress plugins directory: <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li><li>Upload the extracted plugin directory to this folder.</li></ol><p><strong>Step 3: Activate</strong></p><ol><li>Go to your <strong>WordPress Admin → Plugins</strong>.</li><li>Find <strong>Tranzila Payment for WooCommerce POS</strong> in the list.</li><li>Click <strong>Activate</strong>.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="_3-post-installation-checks" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-post-installation-checks"><span>3. Post-Installation Checks</span></a></h2><p>To verify that the plugin has installed successfully:</p><ul><li>Clear your WordPress site cache if you use caching plugins (e.g., W3 Total Cache or WP Super Cache).</li><li>Navigate to <strong>Point of Sale → Settings → Payment</strong> and confirm that <strong>Tranzila Terminal</strong> is now listed in the payment method table.</li><li>Navigate to <strong>Point of Sale → Outlets</strong>, edit an outlet, check the payment methods dropdown, select <strong>Tranzila Terminal</strong>, and verify that the &quot;Tranzila Payment Terminal Settings&quot; input block is injected.</li></ul><blockquote><p>[!WARNING] <strong>WooCommerce POS Dependency:</strong> If you activate this plugin and see error notices in your WordPress dashboard, ensure that Webkul&#39;s <a href="https://wpdoc.webkul.com/pos-for-woocommerce/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">POS for WooCommerce</a> plugin is installed and activated. The addon will gracefully disable its registration hooks if its core dependency is missing.</p></blockquote>',31)])])}]])}}]);